/*!
    \module MemberLink
    \title Member Link Context
    \brief A module that documents the member link context fixture class.
*/

/*!
    \page member_link_context.html
    \title Member Link Context
    \brief Overview of the member link context fixture.

    The alpha and beta members each register the same member-detail
    target, immediately followed by their own section heading. Links to
    member-detail that are authored in a member body or see-also list
    must resolve to the authoring member's own section.

    \keyword beta

    The beta keyword is registered on this page, but member body links
    that spell it out resolve to the sibling member, because a class
    page prioritizes its own hierarchy over this page's keyword.

    The page body of this overview links to the class itself:
    \l MemberLinkContext
*/

/*!
    \qmlmodule MemberLinkQml
    \title Member Link QML
    \brief A QML module that documents the signal origin fixture type.
*/

/*!
    \qmltype SignalOrigins
    \inqmlmodule MemberLinkQml
    \brief A QML type that carries the duplicate signal anchor cases.

    The regular and attached activated() signals each register the same
    signal-detail target, immediately followed by their own section
    heading. Links to signal-detail that are authored in a signal body
    or see-also list must resolve to the authoring signal's own section.
*/

/*!
    \qmlsignal MemberLinkQml::SignalOrigins::activated()
    Regular signal documentation.

    \target signal-detail
    \section1 Regular Notes
    Regular body follows \l signal-detail.
    \sa signal-detail
*/

/*!
    \qmlattachedsignal MemberLinkQml::SignalOrigins::activated()
    Attached signal documentation.

    \target signal-detail
    \section1 Attached Notes
    Attached body follows \l signal-detail.
    \sa signal-detail
*/
